{
  "id": "anthracite_coal",
  "title": "Anthracite Coal",
  "description": "Anthracite coal is available in a number of different grades or sizes. Each size is suited for different sizes of grates and firepots, including buckwheat, egg, stove, chestnut, pea, and broken grades.",
  "type": "calculator-chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Anthracite Coal Grades\n\nAnthracite coal is available in a number of different grades or sizes:\n\n* **Buckwheat** - Used in automatic coal firing burners in domestic, commercial and industrial stokers\n* **Egg** - Used in large firepots, usually with beds more than 16 inches deep\n* **Stove** - Used for heating buildings. Mostly replaced with gas or oil\n* **Chestnut** - Used in medium firepots, usually with beds ranging 10-15 inches\n* **Pea** - Small grade anthracite\n* **Broken** - Broken pieces of anthracite coal\n\nEach size is suited for different sizes of grates and firepots."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "coal_weight",
          "label": "Coal Weight",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "tons",
          "defaultValue": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "coal_grade",
          "label": "Coal Grade",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Buckwheat",
              "value": 0.85
            },
            {
              "label": "Egg",
              "value": 0.9
            },
            {
              "label": "Stove",
              "value": 0.88
            },
            {
              "label": "Chestnut",
              "value": 0.87
            },
            {
              "label": "Pea",
              "value": 0.82
            },
            {
              "label": "Broken",
              "value": 0.8
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "carbon_content",
          "label": "Carbon Content Adjustment",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "%",
          "defaultValue": 95
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "energy_output",
          "label": "Energy Output",
          "unit": "BTU",
          "formula": "inputs.coal_weight * inputs.coal_grade * inputs.carbon_content * 13000",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "efficiency_rating",
          "label": "Efficiency Rating",
          "unit": "%",
          "formula": "inputs.coal_grade * 100",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "headers": [
        "Coal Grade",
        "Efficiency Rating",
        "Typical Firepot Depth"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Buckwheat",
          85,
          "Automatic Burners"
        ],
        [
          "Egg",
          90,
          ">16 inches"
        ],
        [
          "Stove",
          88,
          "General Heating"
        ],
        [
          "Chestnut",
          87,
          "10-15 inches"
        ],
        [
          "Pea",
          82,
          "Small Grates"
        ],
        [
          "Broken",
          80,
          "Variable"
        ]
      ],
      "options": {
        "xAxis": {
          "type": "category",
          "data": [
            "Buckwheat",
            "Egg",
            "Stove",
            "Chestnut",
            "Pea",
            "Broken"
          ]
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "type": "value"
        },
        "series": [
          {
            "data": [
              85,
              90,
              88,
              87,
              82,
              80
            ],
            "type": "bar",
            "name": "Efficiency Rating (%)"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}